## Conventions (personal)
- Prefer small, boring dependencies; justify each new one in the commit body.
- Every repo has a `README.md` with a one-paragraph summary and a "Run it" section.

## Known repos (personal)
- api (personal-api) — Personal JSON API behind the blog and side-tool uploads · /srv/code/api
- blog (site) — Static site; posts in content/, theme in themes/plain · /srv/code/blog
- dotfiles · /srv/code/dotfiles
- side-tool (photos, renamer) — Small CLI that renames photos by EXIF date; Rust, entry point src/main.rs · /srv/code/side-tool · notes: ~/personal-store/repos/side-tool/notes.md

## This repo
Scope: personal.
For any repo above, read its code at the listed path; check its notes first if listed.
Lookup: `kipi where <alias>`, `kipi grep <term> --repos`.
